            <h2 id="agents">Give coding agents the reporter’s machine</h2>
            <div class="pair">
              <div class="pair-text">
                <p>
                  An agent fixing #21538 runs the tests on its own machine, they pass, and it has nothing
                  to work with. twin’s MCP server lets it replay the failure, run commands in the
                  reporter’s environment, try a change, and verify the final diff on a fresh machine.
                </p>
                <p class="small">
                  Recorded session. Select a call to see its result. <a href={docs.agents}>Agent guide</a>
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class="stack">
                <figure class="term">
                  <figcaption><span>Add to Claude Code</span></figcaption>
                  <pre><code><span class="t-dim">$</span> claude mcp add twin -e SOLARI_API_KEY=slr_live_... -- npx -y @crypticsaiyan/twincli mcp</code></pre>
                </figure>
                <figure class="term" data-demo="agents" data-selected={shownCall}>
                  <figcaption>
                    <span>MCP session, ids shortened</span>
                    <span class="cap-meta">
                      <span class="time">{sessionSeconds} s</span>
                      <button type="button" class="again" hidden>Play again</button>
                    </span>
                  </figcaption>
                  <div class="timeline" aria-hidden="true">
                    <div class="track">
                      {calls.map((call, index) => (
                        <span class="seg" data-i={index} style={`flex-grow: ${call.seconds}`} title={`${call.name}, ${call.seconds} s`}>
                          <span class="fill"></span>
                          {call.seconds >= 30 && <span class="seg-label">{call.name}</span>}
                        </span>
                      ))}
                    </div>
                    <div class="scale"><span>0 s</span><span>{sessionSeconds} s</span></div>
                  </div>
                  <ol class="calls">
                    {calls.map((call, index) => (
