                        </button>
                      </li>
                    ))}
                  </ol>
                  <div class="call-out">
                    {calls.map((call, index) => (
                      <pre data-i={index} hidden={index !== shownCall}><code set:html={call.detail} /></pre>
                    ))}
                  </div>
                </figure>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="pair">
              <div class="pair-text">
                <h3>Check the pull request where the bug happens</h3>
                <p>
                  The GitHub Action verifies each pull request in the reporter’s environment and comments
                  the verdict. The check fails unless the bug is fixed.
                </p>
                <p class="small"><a href={docs.action}>Action reference</a></p>
              </div>
              <figure class="term">
                <figcaption><code>.github/workflows/twin.yml</code></figcaption>
                <pre><code>{`on: pull_request
jobs:
  verify:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: crypticsaiyan/twin@main
        with:
          solari-api-key: \${{ secrets.SOLARI_API_KEY }}`}</code></pre>
              </figure>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="band" aria-labelledby="files">
        <div class="col sec">
          <div class="rail"><p><span>05</span> Files</p></div>
          <div class="body split">
            <h2 id="files">What a capsule holds</h2>
            <p class="intro">
              <code>twin-capsule.json</code> is a few kilobytes. The reporter reviews it before it is written.
            </p>
            <div class="cols">
              <div>
                <h3>Recorded</h3>
                <ul>
                  <li>OS, libc and architecture</li>
                  <li>Runtime and package manager versions, lockfile hashes</li>
                  <li>Installed Node and Python package versions</li>
                  <li>Remote, commit, branch and <code>git diff HEAD</code></li>
                  <li>Time zone and locale</li>
                  <li>Values of <code>TZ</code>, <code>NODE_ENV</code>, <code>LANG</code>, <code>CI</code> and a few more</li>
                  <li>Exit status, output tail and a failure fingerprint</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div>
                <h3>Never recorded</h3>
                <ul>
                  <li>Other environment values: names only</li>
                  <li>Tokens, keys and passwords: replaced by pattern and entropy rules</li>
                  <li>Home directory paths: rewritten to <code>~</code></li>
                  <li>Contents of untracked files: names only</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="small"><a href={docs.privacy}>Privacy and redaction</a></p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

